  <section class="lk-section lk-section--white lk-about" id="about">
    <div class="lk-wrap lk-wrap--narrow">
      <h2 class="lk-h2">A quiet resort escape outside Lusaka</h2>
      <p>Lukasa is a genuinely well kept property. The lawns are neatly mowed and there is plenty of shade from big trees, with a tree swing and a climbing frame for kids to enjoy. The toilets and showers are clean and there are enough of them that you are rarely waiting.</p>
      <p>The owners are friendly and easy to talk to, and having a proper swimming pool on site makes the whole stay feel like a real break from the city rather than just a night under canvas. Because the property is set back from the main road, it is remarkably quiet.</p>
      <p>It is the kind of place where you can do as much or as little as you like. If you are camping, you generally look after your own meals, but book a room instead and breakfast is included, with dinner available on request, so you can turn up with little more than an overnight bag if you want to.</p>
      <p>Evenings by the fire pit are lovely, the night sky is properly dark once you are away from the lights, and both sunrise and sunset over the grounds are worth getting up, or staying out, for.</p>
      <p>One thing worth knowing before you go: there are several dogs living on the property. They wander around the camping area and may follow you around after dark, so keep this in mind if you are not entirely comfortable around dogs.</p>
      <p>It is not the cheapest campsite around Lusaka, but for the resort comforts you get in return, most visitors will feel it is worth it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

